# qwen3-8b-jetson — Qwen3-8B for the mt100 board, instruct mode
#
# Build:   ollama create qwen3-8b-jetson -f infra/ollama/Modelfile.qwen3-8b-jetson
# Profile: apps/llm/model_profiles.py ("local_ollama/qwen3-8b-jetson")
#
# WHY A TAG AND NOT JUST THE PROFILE — model_profiles can only pin num_ctx on
# requests built by our own Ollama client. The grader's Tier-2 verifier reaches
# Ollama through instructor.from_provider('ollama'), i.e. the OpenAI-compatible
# /v1/chat/completions endpoint, which has no num_ctx field. Ollama keys a
# runner on (model, params), so the verifier's call lands at the 4096 default —
# a different runner from the tutor's 16384 — and under
# OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 that evicts the tutor and reloads it. A Modelfile
# PARAMETER applies on every endpoint, which is the only fix that covers paths
# we do not construct requests for.
#
# INSTRUCT MODE. qwen3:8b is a HYBRID template that gates on the Think flag, so
# the profile's ollama_think=False genuinely suppresses reasoning here (unlike
# qwen3:4b Thinking-2507, where the flag only disables Ollama's parser). There
# is no separate qwen3:8b-instruct tag to build from, so the flag is the
# mechanism — keep the profile and this file in agreement.
FROM qwen3:8b

# Must match local_ollama/qwen3-8b-jetson in apps/llm/model_profiles.py.
# If the two disagree, the disagreement IS the bug.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Qwen3's recommended instruct sampling, restated so the tag is
# self-describing and the OpenAI-compatible path gets them too.
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
